From c233b744cc3eacd85bef4fa5159d39552e22a743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:40:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a pool can keep its order through a short rest
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wssz527 (#4030): a Kimi Code subscription answers 429 "The engine is
currently overloaded" for seconds at a time. restLast moved the resting
account behind the pool's other one whatever the routing had ordered, so
the conversation moved and paid its whole prompt again on the next
account, and again on coming back — on their log, 10 of 35 overloaded
429s moved accounts in 20 days, and a cache read costs a rounding error
where an uncached prompt costs a large multiple. No setting kept a
resting account in front, and stays=strict hands the 429 to the agent
even when a long window is genuinely spent.

- provider.go: KeepThroughRest, off by default, says a transient rest is
  no reason to move a provider's keys or accounts; accountSettings copies
  it with the pool's other settings (#4738's one list both ways).
- routing.go: SetKeepThroughRest, beside SetCapStop and SetCapCareful.
- fallback.go: restLast asks candidate.keepsThrough — a rate limit or a
  failure that says nothing of why keeps its place, which the routing
  ordered, and its trace row still says it rests, so a new conversation
  goes to a ready one (readyForNew). Quota, credit, restriction and
  verification still move it, as does every rest of a provider without
  the setting.
- pool_cli.go: `magpie provider pool <id> --keep on|off`, and the pool's
  lines say what keep through a rest does.
- providers.go: a save from the provider editor keeps KeepThroughRest,
  as it does CapStop and CapCareful, so a value set from the CLI is not
  lost.
- docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md: a bullet beside restLast's.

Tests (pool_keep_test.go; pool_keep_cli_test.go):
- TestPoolKeepsThroughARateRest: a keeping pool's account resting out of
  a rate limit, or after a failure, is asked where the routing put it,
  ahead of a ready one, and the trace says its rest; nothing promotes it
  past a ready one either.
- TestPoolStillMovesOnQuotaAndWithoutTheSetting: quota and credit still
  move it, and a rate rest moves it for a provider without the setting.
- TestPoolKeepSaysItsPoolKeepsThroughARest: --keep on, --keep off, and
  --keep maybe refused.
- TestAccountSettingsKept keeps and clears it on a signed-in account,
  as the rests' settings are.

Fixes #4030

